  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Phat phrik khing serves 4 and takes about 25 minutes. Unlike a wet curry, there is no coconut milk here. The red curry paste coats the pork and the green beans (use 200 g of trimmed green beans, no slug, describe in method) and the dish finishes dry and aromatic. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kaffir lime leaves",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kaffir-lime-leaves"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " are shredded finely and added at the end."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fry the curry paste until it is fragrant and the oil separates before adding the pork. This is the step that cooks out the raw flavour of the paste and makes the dish deeply savoury."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
